          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %strong principal ideal domain
            if it satisfies any of these equivalent conditions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal"} principal ideal
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unique+factorization+domain"} unique factorization domain
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout domain
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout domain
                which satisfies the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ascending+chain+condition+on+principal+ideals"} ascending chain condition on principal ideals
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+domain"} atomic domain
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                has a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind-Hasse+norm"} Dedekind-Hasse norm
          %p
            Often
            %em pid
            is used as an abbreviation of “principal ideal domain”.
          %p
            To show that definitions (2-4) are equivalent, consider that unique factorization domains and Noetherian domains both satisfy the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ascending+chain+condition+on+principal+ideals"} ascending chain condition on principal ideals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GCD+domain"} GCD domain
            which satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ascending+chain+condition+on+principal+ideals"} ascending chain condition on principal ideals
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unique+factorization+domain"} unique factorization domain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domains"} Bézout domains
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GCD+domains"} GCD domains
          %p Now to show that definitions 1 is equivalent to (2-4). Every integral domain whose ideals are principal is a Bézout domain by considering the ideals which are finitely generated. To show that these are Noetherian domains and unique factorization domains, we have the following:
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              In a integral domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              whose ideals are principal, an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is irreducible iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+ideal"} maximal ideal
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is irreducible and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∉
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \notin (x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, x
              is principal, say
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = b y
              and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is irreducible, one of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b, y
              is a unit; if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is a unit then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x) = (b) = (a, x)
              and thus
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in (x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              must be a unit, i.e.,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (b)
              is the improper ideal. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              has no proper extension:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              is maximal.
            %p
              For any ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              is maximal and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = a b
              for a non-unit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x) \subseteq (a)
              is an equality by maximality, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = x v
              for some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi x
                      %mi v
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = x v b
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi v
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = v b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              is a unit.
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              An integral domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              whose ideals are principal is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The union of an ascending chain of ideals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_1 \subseteq I_2 \subseteq \ldots
              is an ideal
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = (x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              belongs to one of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I = I_n
          %p
            Thus, an integral domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            whose ideals are principal is a Noetherian Bézout domain.
          %p Similarly,
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              An integral domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              whose ideals are principal is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unique+factorization+domain"} unique factorization domain
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Working in classical logic, Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#noeth"}
              says that the reverse inclusion relation on the set of nonzero ideals is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-founded+relation"} well-founded
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be the subset of ideals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a)
              that are products of finitely many (maybe zero!) maximal principal ideals. For any proper ideal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x) \neq (0)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t)
              properly containing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              can be factored into maximals, then so can
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              is maximal/irreducible, or factors as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s)(t)
              where both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              are non-units;
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t)
              factor into maximals by hypothesis, and therefore so does
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an inductive set, so by well-foundedness it contains every ideal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≠
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x) \neq (0)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              can be factored into irreducibles.
            %p
              For uniqueness of the factorization, we first remark that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is irreducible and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p|a b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p|a
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p|b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/(p)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              and thus
              %em a fortiori
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≡
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b \equiv 0 \; mod p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi mod
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \equiv 0 \; mod p
              or
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≡
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi mod
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \equiv 0 \; mod p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mi …
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi m
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mn 2
                    %mi …
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1 p_2 \ldots p_m = q_1 q_2 \ldots q_n
              are two factorizations into irreducibles of the same element, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
              divides one of the irreducibles
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_1) = (q_i)
              and each is a unit times the other, meaning we can cancel
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
              on both sides and argue by induction.
          %p
            Thus, an integral domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            whose ideals are principal is a Bézout unique factorization domain.
          %p It remains to show using classical logic that every ideal of a Noetherian Bézout domain or a Bézout UFD is a principal ideal… (to be done)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %li
              %p
                the ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
                in a field (in fact, for any commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[x]
                is a pid if and
                %em only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
