                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+domain"} Euclidean domain
            %li
              %p
                in the ring of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+function"} entire
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
                every finitely generated ideal is principal (
                %a{:href => "#Helmer40"}> Helmer 40
                ), but the ring is only a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout domain
          %p
            That both the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+rings"} polynomial rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q[x]
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+fields"} finite fields
            are principal integral domains with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            is one aspect of the close similarity between the two that is the topic of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout domain
            may then be viewed as part of the further similarity that relates the previous two to topics such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+duality"} geometric Langlands duality
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy+--+table"} function field analogy – table
            for more on this.
          %h2#StructureTheoryOfModules Structure theory of modules
          %h3#free_and_projective_modules Free and projective modules
          #free.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a pid, then any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submodule"} submodule
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is also free. (For the converse statement, see
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/free+module#submod"} here
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By freeness of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \cong \sum_{j \in J} R_j
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              of copies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_j
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              (as a module over the ring
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-ordering"} well-ordered
              using the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\leq j} \coloneqq \sum_{i \leq j} R_i, \qquad F_{\lt j} \coloneqq \sum_{i \lt j} R_i\,.
            %p
              Any element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \cap F_{\leq j}
              can be written uniquely as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, r)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in F_{\lt j}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R_j
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_j \colon M \cap F_{\leq j} \to R
            %p
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_j((x, r)) = r
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_j
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mrow
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \cap F_{\lt j}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} im
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi j
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to M \cap F_{\lt j} \to M \cap F_{\leq j} \to \im p_j \to 0
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} im
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \im p_j
              is a submodule (i.e., an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subseteq J
              consist of those
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi j
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_j \neq 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_k
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_k(m_k) = r_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{m_k: k \in K\}
              forms a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %p
              First we prove
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+independence"} linear independence
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{m_k\}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i=1}^{n} a_i m_{k_i} = 0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                      %mo &lt;
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi …
                      %mo &lt;
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_1 \lt k_2 \lt \ldots \lt k_n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_{k_n}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n p_{k_n}(m_{k_n}) = a_n r_{k_n} = 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi k
                            %mi n
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_{k_n} \neq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_n = 0
              (since we are working over a domain). The assertion now follows by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            %p
              Now we prove that the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_k
              generate
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in J
              be the least
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              such that some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi j
