          %h3#torsionfree_modules Torsion-free modules
          #torsionfree.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A finitely generated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsionfree
              module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              over a pid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is free.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a finite set of generators of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subseteq S
              be a maximal subset of linearly independent elements. (Unless
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              has at least one element, because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is torsionfree.) We claim that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              can be embedded as a submodule of the free module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              (which in turn is the span of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              as a submodule
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq M
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#free"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is free.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1, \ldots, x_n
              be the elements of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                      %mo −
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \in S - T
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi m
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi …
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_m m + r_1 x_1 + \ldots + r_n x_n = 0
            %p
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi m
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_m \neq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              in the complement
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo −
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S - T
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_m
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi S
                          %mo −
                          %mi T
                      %msub
                        %mi r
                        %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = \prod_{m \in S - T} r_m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_r \colon M \to M
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to \lambda_r(M)
              is monic because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is torsionfree. This completes the proof.
          #flat.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be a pid. Then an
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is torsionfree if and only if it is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+module"} flat
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is flat. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be the field of fractions of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a domain, we have a monic
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo →
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \to K
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %mi K
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi R
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \cong R \otimes_R M \to K \otimes_R M
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %mi M
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi r
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊗
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi r
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi M
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi R
                            %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    M &amp; \to &amp; K \otimes_R M \\
                    \\mathllap{\lambda_r} \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{1 \otimes \lambda_r} \\
                    M &amp; \to &amp; K \otimes_R M
                    }
            %p
              commutes, and since the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \otimes \lambda_r
              is multiplication by a non-zero scalar on a vector space, it follows that this map and therefore also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_r
              is monic, i.e.,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is torsionfree.
            %p
              In the other direction, suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is torsionfree. Any module is the filtered colimit over the system of finitely generated submodules and inclusions between them; in this case all the finitely generated submodules of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              are torsion-free and hence free, by Proposition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#torsionfree"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a filtered colimit of free modules; it is therefore flat by a standard result proved
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/flat+module#filtfree"} here
          %h3#structure_theory_of_finitely_generated_modules Structure theory of finitely generated modules
          %p
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+theorem+for+finitely+generated+modules+over+a+principal+ideal+domain"} structure theorem for finitely generated modules over a principal ideal domain
          %h2#InConstructiveMathematics In constructive mathematics
          %p
            First of all, in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domains"} integral domains
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+integral+domains"} Heyting integral domains
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+integral+domains"} discrete integral domains
            %em Heyting principal ideal domains
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em discrete principal ideal domains
          %p In addition, the various definitions of principal ideal domains do not coincide with each other in constructive mathematics. For example, consider the classically true equivalence of discrete Bézout unique factorization domains and discrete integral domains where every ideal is principal:
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+integral+domain"} discrete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9zout+domain"} Bézout
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unique+factorization+domain"} unique factorization domain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ideal"} principal ideal
              if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} law of excluded middle
              holds.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              In one direction, the usual proofs rely on being able to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+proposition"} decide
              whether any particular element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              belongs to the ideal or not. For the converse, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
              be an arbitrary proposition. Consider the ideal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ x \in R | (x = 0) \vee \varphi \}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+integral+domain"} discrete integral domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = 0
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\varphi
              holds, in the second
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
          %p
            It is unknown whether in the absence of excluded middle, there are Heyting integral domains where every ideal is a principal ideal. But with Heyting integral domains, maybe we should be talking about
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+anti-ideal"} principal anti-ideal
              domains
            instead of principal ideal domains.
